'''Jumbo Jones''' (ジャンボーグ鈴木, ''Janbōgu Suzuki'', '''Jumborg Suzuki''') is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of [[Sunfish Jones]] that appears in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Jumbo Invasion]]. He was added in [[Version 14.6 Update|Version 14.6]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Jumbo Jones
|image = E 743.png
|appearance = [[Jumbo Invasion]]
|money drop = 4,000¢ - 15,800¢
}}

==Enemy==
A Great [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] version of [[Sunfish Jones]] with extremely high stats that exchanges range and support for speed and pure pushing power. He has a 2-part attack with [[Omni Strike]] on the (relatively weak) 1st hit and what is effectively [[Long Distance]] on the 2nd hit, heavily punishing any units standing beyond 451 range with 90k damage, a level 7 [[Wave Attack]] and a 2-second [[Slow]].

Unlike Sunfish Jones, Jumbo Jones' delay between attacks consists solely of backswing, so he will always start attacking again should he flinch.

==Strategy==
Jumbo Jones is best treated as a Long Distance enemy with a minimum range of 450, as his damage output up close is manageable unless he manages to land the second hit and fire his Wave. The best way to fight him is with fast or bulky melee units able to withstand the close-ranged hits and prevent him from pushing, particularly those [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|immune to Waves]] or possessing [[Wave Shield]] to neutralize the incoming Wave even if he manages to land his second attack. His Slow effect can occasionally be troublesome, but has a low enough uptime to be completely manageable.

While Jumbo Jones is immune to Freeze, he is still vulnerable to [[Knockback]] and Sniper, which, along with other DPS sources, can force him to repeatedly flinch and delay or prevent his attacks outright.

