==Trivia==
*Since [[Sunfish Jones]]'s description references an aircraft (the Northrop Grumman [[wikipedia:Northrop Grumman B-2 Spirit|B-2 Spirit]] stealth bomber), Jumbo Jones's name may reference [[wikipedia:Jumbo jet|jumbo jets]].
*Jumbo Jones's Japanese name, Jumborg Suzuki (ジャンボーグ鈴木 ''Janbōgu Suzuki'') is derived from ''jumbo'', ''Manborg Suzuki'' (マンボーグ鈴木 ''Manbōgu Suzuki'', Sunfish Jones's Japanese name) and possibly the ''[[wikipedia:Tokusatsu|tokusatsu]]'' series ''[[wikipedia:Jumborg Ace|Jumborg Ace]]''. The series' main giant mechas are the titular [[wikia:ultra:Jumborg Ace (mecha)|Jumborg Ace]], who has a maximum flight speed of Mach 11 (i.e., 11 times the speed of sound) and later [[wikia:ultra:Jumborg 9|Jumborg 9]], who can attain similar speeds when running, which may be why Jumbo Jones has such high movement speed.
*Since most of the other [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]] appear to have religious inspirations, Jumbo Jones may represent [[wikipedia:Leviathan|Leviathan]], a biblical sea monster associated with chaos and the sin of envy. Leviathan is known for being extremely large, and the largest extant bony fish are the [[wikipedia:Giant sunfish|giant sunfish]] followed by the [[wikipedia:Ocean sunfish|ocean sunfish]]. In some [[wikipedia:Classification of demons|classifications of demons]], Leviathan is one of the princes of Hell alongside Satan and Lucifer, who may be represented by [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]] and [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] respectively.
**In this regard, Jumbo Jones can be seen as a foil to [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|Sea Serpent Daliasan]], an [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] Colossus Slayer whose name may be partially derived from Leviathan. Daliasan has horns and a [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] face on its Evolved Form's tail, suggesting a demon, but is on the player's side, whereas Jumbo Jones is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], perhaps representing the interpretation of Leviathan as simply another of God's creations, but is on the enemies' side. Both also have Long Distance and Slow abilities.
**The [[Media:Bg016.png|ruined city background]] in [[Aqua Saint I (Deadly)|Aqua Saint I]] may imply that an apocalypse has occurred, which could be a reference to Leviathan being defeated at the end of time.
**Jumbo Jones could also represent the great fish sent by God to transport [[wikipedia:Jonah|Jonah]] by swallowing him, as the phrase 大聖魚 ''Daisēgyo'' in his stages' Japanese names literally translates to "Great Holy Fish" or "Large Holy Fish".
*The orbs of electricity in Jumbo Jones's attack animation may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Ball lightning|ball lightning]], a rare and unexplained atmospheric phenomenon best described as luminescent, spherical objects that appear during or shortly after thunderstorms.
*The Colossus jewel being embedded in Jumbo Jones's forehead may be a reference to the nuchal humps that grow in the foreheads of some fish species, such as the [[wikipedia:Flowerhorn cichlid|flowerhorn cichlid]]. A nuchal hump is made of fat and stores calories.
*Jumbo Jones has a "King" title like the first three Great Advent Bosses, but only in the [[Media:Eve l 246 nyanko images MSTm2PwFwoiA14wl1BuB.png|Japanese event poster]] for [[Jumbo Invasion]]. His title is "King Who Sprang from the Deep Sea" (深海を飛び出した王 ''Shinkai o Tobidashita Ō''), which is changed to "Lord of the Deep" in the [[Media:Eve l 183 en.png|English event poster]].

